    "blurb": "The second set erupts with a blazing He’s Gone → Truckin’ → The Other One → Spanish Jam sequence and an out‑of‑space I Know You Rider. Jerry delivers incendiary riffs and a top‑form solo on Tennessee Jed, while Phil drives the jams with thumping bass. Recording quality is solid soundboard with crisp instrument separation.",
    "review": "On March 31 1973 at Buffalo’s War Memorial Auditorium the Dead turned in a high‑energy performance that still feels fresh. The first set was relaxed but solid, highlighted by a fiery Tennessee Jed solo and a tight Playing In The Band. Then the second set kicked into overdrive: a monster He’s Gone → Truckin’ → The Other One → Spanish Jam stretch flows seamlessly into an unexpected I Know You Rider out of space before closing with a bright Sugar Magnolia. Jerry’s Roy‑Buchanan‑like tone, Phil’s driving bass, and Bill’s heavy snare/tom presence keep the momentum soaring, while Keith’s keyboards sit nicely in the mix adding texture without overpowering. The soundboard capture is crisp and balanced, with only minor tape hiss, making this show a must‑listen for fans of ’73 Dead.",
